// Costa Bits: a sunset run round a bay of the Andalusian coast. The lap
// goes clockwise round the bay, out over the mountains on the open sea and
// back along the south coast, over the bay's outlet and through a fork
// before the line.
//
// 1. Salida / Recta costera: the start straight runs north along the bay's
//    west shore, a railing, palms and the water on the right, the town's
//    whitewashed houses on the left.
// 2. Curvas del acantilado: S-bends climbing north up the cliffs, cut rock
//    on the left, the bay below on the right, to some 27 m.
// 3. Túnel de la montaña: round to the east at the head of the bay, and
//    through the mountain behind it in a tunnel.
// 4. Out of the tunnel, south down the bay's east shore, and east over the
//    headland through a pine forest to the open sea.
// 5. Carretera de la sierra: a mountain road south up the cliffs over the
//    open sea, cut rock on the right, a stone parapet over the drop on the
//    left; through a gorge, the town's houses on its rims and an old stone
//    bridge high over the road, which runs under its arch; to a summit some 56 m up, on a straight, where the bike takes
//    off; then down in bends round the cape, its watchtower far below, and
//    off the mountain to the south coast.
// 6. Autopista de la costa: a straight west along the south coast over two
//    crests in a row, the bike in the air over each flat out, palms close on
//    both sides, the sea on the left; and the Puente costero, over the bay's
//    outlet to the sea.
// 7. La bifurcación: round to the right, north, and the road splits before
//    the line: a way to the left over a hump, the lap swinging out to the
//    right, both as quick, and they meet again on the start straight.
//
// Where things are, in metres from the finish line:
//
// - the start straight:      Span(4214.0, 340.0), a crest at 155 m
// - the cliffs:              Span(380.0, 930.0)
// - the tunnel:              Span(985.0, 1150.0)
// - the east shore:          Span(1230.0, 1540.0)
// - over the headland:       Span(1540.0, 2040.0), through the forest
// - up the mountain road:    Span(2040.0, 2500.0), the summit at 2500 m
//   - the gorge:             Span(2110.0, 2320.0), the bridge over it at 2215 m
// - down round the cape:     Span(2540.0, 3174.0)
//   - narrow, under the rock: Span(2740.0, 3105.0)
// - the coast highway:       Span(3174.0, 3444.0), crests at 3230 and 3340 m,
//                            the lighthouse beside it at 3250 m, at (525.0, 704.0)
// - the bridge:              Span(3444.0, 3650.0), over the outlet, 165 m wide
// - the fork:                Span(3864.0, 4214.0)
//
// How a circuit's file is written: see the engine's src/circuits/data.rs.
(
    name: "Costa Bits",
    name_en: "Costa Bits",
